{"label":"We should be providing a query string module but optionally allowing the user to bring their own (maybe via setting when creating the app or something","date":"2014-07-07T02:27:13Z","author":"defunctzombie","url":"https://github.com/expressjs/express/issues/2215#issuecomment-48135987","context":"issue #2215","body":"We should be providing a query string module but optionally allowing the user to bring their own (maybe via setting when creating the app or something)

We can do what @jonathanong suggested or optionally think about

``` js
var app = express({ qs: my_qs });
```

I know we haven't passed options to express like this before but maybe it could work."}

{"label":"Yes, the plan is to disable by default in Express 5.0. You can view the 5.0 plan here: https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/2237 > Make query par","date":"2017-07-11T05:55:48Z","author":"dougwilson","url":"https://github.com/expressjs/express/issues/3361#issuecomment-314331725","context":"issue #3361","body":"Yes, the plan is to disable by default in Express 5.0. You can view the 5.0 plan here: https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/2237

> Make query parser option default to 'simple'

I hope this helps! I even updated the plan to reference this issues in the check list for that entry, since there wasn't a specific issue before that I recall, just discussions."}

{"label":"I would like a reassessment of the proposed changes in this PR - specifically, on the deprecation in `4.x` part - is this still valid, given we are in","date":"2020-03-06T14:13:31Z","author":"gireeshpunathil","url":"https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/3621#issuecomment-595785463","context":"issue #3621","body":"I would like a reassessment of the proposed changes in this PR - specifically, on the deprecation in `4.x` part - is this still valid, given we are in the brink of 5?

@czaarek99 - are you in position to progress on this PR, collaborating with the community reviewers? this is tagged as an important item that needs to be included in 5.

If yes, let me know if you need any help 
If not, no worries, I am willing to take this up and move forward"}

{"label":"> I would like a reassessment of the proposed changes in this PR - specifically, on the deprecation in 4.x part - is this still valid, given we are in","date":"2020-03-06T14:34:27Z","author":"dougwilson","url":"https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/3621#issuecomment-595794644","context":"issue #3621","body":"> I would like a reassessment of the proposed changes in this PR - specifically, on the deprecation in 4.x part - is this still valid, given we are in the brink of 5?

Since 4.x is still going to exist for quite some time once 5 is released it is still valid. If it doesn't get deprecated in 4 before releasing 5, then it would need to be deprecated in 5 and then released in 6. This is trying to follow the Node.js model, which we have been doing so far for anything that can possibly be marked as deprecated. 

If it is not possible to add a deprecation to 4, then we can reevaluate deprecation, though I don't think that is what you are saying here."}
